WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.302
This slide brings Module 1 together.

00:00:02.302 --> 00:00:05.782
Review the patterns you can now recognize and reuse.

00:00:05.782 --> 00:00:11.532
Focus on the decisions behind the syntax: what structure or method fits the problem,

00:00:11.532 --> 00:00:16.272
what assumptions are being made, and what you should check before trusting the result.

00:00:16.272 --> 00:00:19.457
Connect the concept to a small analytics task.

00:00:19.457 --> 00:00:24.532
Imagine the value came from a sales file, survey, or operational system.

00:00:24.532 --> 00:00:30.662
Ask whether Python is interpreting it correctly and whether another person could understand the calculation

00:00:30.662 --> 00:00:32.137
from the names and output.

00:00:32.137 --> 00:00:37.907
Before moving on, explain the main idea in one sentence without reading the slide.

00:00:37.907 --> 00:00:43.325
That quick explanation is a useful check that the concept is becoming reusable knowledge.
